{
  "source": "skill-sprites.zip from hsextract (sprite-fx.json, same build as data/skill-fx.json): Draw events, sprite origins and animation speeds. speed = sprite frames per game frame; lift = px drawn above the object (yy); ground = shadow under a falling object; slant = drawn at x + height (Comet's diagonal fall); heightScale/heightAlpha = added per px of height; add = bm_add; fades = alpha runs out with the object's fade; circle = bent round its object as draw_sprite_circle bends it (radius and width in px, times the object's scale, floored); steady = plays with the loop, as an object the game never restarts (the player's shadow); fixed = keeps its size whatever its object's scale; first = the frame shown at `from`, for animations an object drives by hand (Exo_Scorching_Whip_obj's imageIndex climbs 10 / 26.4 a frame from its Alarm_0, holds 6 while its lifetime lasts and climbs to 9); flips = mirrored top to bottom while its object points between 90 and 270 deg (yScale -1); a turned layer whose object scales it unevenly or flips is spun: scaled along its own axes before the turn, one frame at a time. Left out: rotation (aim is 0), random start frames (0), Explosion_Item_obj's random -30..30 turn and pulse ring, Fire Ball trails, Meteor shreds, Volcano fragments, Storm Cloud's lightning ring and its cloud 180 px up (outside the view).",
